# What `railway up` uploads.
#
# The repository is a Medplum monorepo and runs to several gigabytes; the
# worker's Dockerfile needs a small fraction of it. Uploading the rest times
# out before a build ever starts, which reads as a Railway failure rather than
# as "you sent three gigabytes".
#
# Keep this in step with docker/worker.Dockerfile: anything the Dockerfile
# COPYs must not be excluded here.

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
# NOT dist/: the worker imports @medplum/core and @medplum/fhirtypes as
# workspace packages, and resolves them to their built output. Excluding dist
# uploads a context the Dockerfile cannot build from.
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
coverage/
**/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Documentation, the web apps and the other example projects are not part of
# the worker image.
